  "about": "Which model each agent should use with each provider, and what was actually tested. 'model' is the recommendation; 'tested' lists only runs that really happened. A recommendation without a tested entry is a recommendation without a check. Model ids are exactly as the provider names them; an empty id with codex means the Codex CLI's own default model. Prices are in prices.json. openrouter: the same models through OpenRouter, ids as OpenRouter names them. claude_code: the Claude Code CLI signed in with the person's own subscription; frames are not passed to it, so agents that read frames do not use it. ollama: local models in Ollama on the person's own computer (stage 20): ids as `ollama pull` takes them; size_gb is the download, vram_gb the video memory it wants; local models are weaker than the cloud ones and none was tested yet. Models smaller than 7B are not recommended: they break the JSON.",
